xt"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}]},{"text":"Required-reason APIs","anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessed